AI Interview Questions for a Java Developer with 10 Years of Experience — 2026


Recommended preparation order
For your Java interview preparation, focus first on these areas rather than attempting to learn all 200 questions at once.

Priority 1 — Java + Spring Boot AI integration
Questions 46–65
Learn how to call an LLM, create an AI service, validate outputs, handle timeouts, and test the integration.

Priority 2 — RAG
Questions 66–85
Understand document chunking, embeddings, vector search, retrieval, grounding, and permission enforcement.

Priority 3 — Microservices and resilience
Questions 116–130
Prepare timeouts, circuit breakers, Kafka, asynchronous processing, scaling, and fallback strategies.

Priority 4 — Security and production
Questions 131–175
Prepare prompt injection, PII protection, cost controls, testing, evaluation, and observability.

Priority 5 — System design and leadership
Questions 186–200
Practise explaining architecture, trade-offs, business value, production risks, and design decisions.


For a senior Java Full Stack Developer, AI interview questions are increasingly relevant because enterprise applications are integrating Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), AI agents, and AI-powered APIs.
At 10 years of experience, interviewers may evaluate not only AI definitions, but also how you integrate AI with Spring Boot, design secure and scalable systems, handle failures, control costs, and deploy AI features in production.
Below is a structured question bank of 200 AI interview questions, organized by topic and difficulty.
